      {
         "id": "c",
         "prompt": "Find \\( H'(x) \\), and find the value of \\( H'\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right) \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "H'\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right) = \\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{2}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Product rule, with the chain rule on the square root.",
               "latex": "H'(x) = 2x\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}} + x^{2} \\cdot \\frac{-2x}{2\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}} = 2x\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}} - \\frac{x^{3}}{\\sqrt{9 - x^{2}}}"
            },
            {
               "text": "At x = sqrt(5) the root is 2.",
               "latex": "H'\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right) = 2\\sqrt{5} \\cdot 2 - \\frac{5\\sqrt{5}}{2} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{2}"
            }
         ],
